{
  "info": {
    "name": "DabApp – Mobile: Course Booking (Full Scenario)",
    "_postman_id": "dabapp-mobile-course-booking-v1",
    "description": "## Mobile Course Booking — Full End-to-End Scenario\n\nBuilt specifically for the mobile app's native PayTabs SDK flow (no browser redirect). Covers: find a course → book (multiple sessions, one payment) → pay via the SDK and verify it yourself → track the booking → trainer starts each session directly (no code needed), then completes it with the trainee's Completion OTP → trainee reviews.\n\nRun the folders **in order** (Phase 1 → 7). Phase 8 contains optional negative/edge-case tests — do NOT run it as part of the main sequence.\n\n### Mobile vs Web — what's different here\n- **Prices are in AED** (`total_price_aed`), not the course's display currency (SAR). Always send `total_price_aed` to the PayTabs SDK — never `total_price`.\n- **You verify your own payment.** After the SDK reports a result, call `POST /trainer/course-bookings/verify-payment` yourself with the `tran_ref` it gave you (Phase 4). This is the mobile-only equivalent of the web flow's server-to-server webhook.\n- **`/trainer/course-bookings/payments/callback` and `/payments/return` are NOT for you.** Those are the web/PayTabs-hosted-page flow only (server-to-server webhook + browser redirect) — the mobile app must never call them.\n- **A declined/unverifiable payment does not cancel the booking.** It stays `confirmed` with `payment_status: failed` for a **2-hour grace window**, during which you can retry (Phase 4-alt, `POST .../pay`) using the same `course_booking_id`. If nothing is confirmed within 2 hours, a backend job auto-cancels it.\n\n### Before you run this\n1. Set `base_url` (defaults to production — point at your own environment if testing locally).\n2. Fill in `trainee_email`/`trainee_password` and `trainer_email`/`trainer_password` with real accounts in your environment.\n3. `trainer_id` / `course_id` default to `6` / `1` — change if your environment doesn't have that data, then re-check Phase 1 step 1-3 (Course Detail) for `total_sessions`, and adjust `session_1_date`/`session_2_date` to match.\n4. `session_1_date` / `session_2_date` go stale over time — if they're in the past, run Phase 1 step 1-5 (Availability) first and pick two fresh, distinct dates.\n5. Phase 4 uses `skip_verification: true` by default so you can run this collection without a live PayTabs sandbox transaction — it exercises the exact same `sdk_trust` fallback path the real app hits when the query API is briefly unreachable. Phase 4-alt shows the real-verification request shape (requires a genuine `tran_ref` from an actual SDK transaction).\n\n### Variables saved automatically as you go\n| Variable | Saved by |\n|---|---|\n| `trainee_token` | Phase 2-1 Login |\n| `trainer_token` | Phase 2-2 Login |\n| `course_total_sessions` / `course_price_aed` | Phase 1-3 Course Detail |\n| `course_booking_id` / `booking_price_aed` | Phase 3-1 Book Course |\n| `session_1_id` / `session_1_start_otp` / `session_1_completion_otp` | Phase 3-2 My Course Bookings |\n| `session_2_id` / `session_2_start_otp` / `session_2_completion_otp` | Phase 3-2 My Course Bookings |\n\n### Key things this scenario proves\n- Both Course Detail and Book Course responses carry `total_price_aed` (Phase 1-3, Phase 3-1).\n- `verify-payment` is idempotent — calling it again on an already-paid booking just confirms, it never double-charges or double-creates a payout (Phase 4-3).\n- A declined verification leaves the booking retryable, not cancelled (Phase 8-1/8-2 exercise this explicitly).\n- OTPs are only ever visible to the trainee's own endpoints — Phase 6 (trainer) never contains `start_otp`/`completion_otp`.\n- The course booking only reaches `completed` once every session is completed (checked in Phase 7-1).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
